  <!-- ORIENTATION -->
    <SplitPanel id="homeless_orientation" title="Introduction" sizes="65,35">
      <LeftPane>
          <Markdown id="homeless_orientation_md">
**Introduction**

Imagine that as part of your degree requirements, you are completing an internship at a local
nonprofit called **Community 360**, or **Comm360** for short.

The mission of Comm360 is to address community-based needs and issues through responsive
programming in multiple areas such as:
 - Education and Training
 - Health and Wellness
 - Family and Youth Services
 - Community Building and Advocacy

A community needs survey conducted by Comm360 identified the high rate of housing insecurity,
specifically homelessness, in the area as a serious issue. You have been asked to work with
other interns to investigate the causes of homelessness to better understand the problem so
that Comm360 can explore ways to address it.
          </Markdown>
      </LeftPane>
      <RightPane>
          <Image id="homeless_image_nonprofit" src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/nonprofit.png" alt="Nonprofit" />
          <Image id="homeless_image_wordcloud" src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/wordcloud.png" alt="Helping, volunteer, community, donations ..." />
      </RightPane>
    </SplitPanel>

    <Image id="homeless_plaza_image"
         src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/GSU_Library_Plaza.jpg"
         alt="GSU Library Plaza. Photograph by Hwi Padam, CC by SA 4.0"
         height="400px"
    />

    <Markdown id="homeless_task_list">
## Task Outline

Over three parts of this Scenario-based Activity (SBA), you will work with your teammates to
complete the following tasks:
 1. _Brainstorm causes for homelessness._
 2. _Review community focus group data._
 3. _Select focus areas._
 4. _Reflect: Is this an interdisciplinary problem?_
 5. _Review the literature._
 6. _Integrate disciplinary insights and share the results._

This is Part One. In Parts Two and Three you will complete the rest of the interdisciplinary
research process.
    </Markdown>

    <Image id="homeless_brainstorming_image"
         src="/sba/interdisciplinary/images/team_workshop.jpg"
         height="400px"
         alt="Talking about processes at a team brainstorming session. Source: UCT MOOC, CC by SA 4.0 International License" />

    <Markdown id="homeless_internal_and_structural_causes">
## Individual and Structural Causes

 - **Individual-level causes** arise from **a person's own experiences or situation**;
     for instance, an untreated mental health condition or a sudden job loss can make it
     harder to maintain stable housing.
 - **Structural causes** arise from **outside the individual**, from the way that
     housing markets, the economy, and community institutions are organized; for
     instance, when affordable-housing supply does not keep up with demand, even
     people with stable jobs can be priced out.
    </Markdown>

