_Select the causes you think are most important to research._

**Choose at least three but no more than five.**
      </Markdown>
      <CheckboxInput id="hl_reasons">
        <Key id="reason_trauma" value="Trauma and untreated mental health">Trauma — domestic violence, family conflict, or untreated mental health conditions — leading to housing insecurity</Key>
        <Key id="reason_records" value="Eviction and criminal records">Eviction filings and minor charges in tenant screening databases that lead landlords to deny applications</Key>
        <Key id="reason_economic" value="Limited economic opportunity">Limited economic opportunity and restrictive labor-market conditions</Key>
        <Key id="reason_affordable" value="Lack of affordable housing">Not enough affordable housing for low- and middle-income residents</Key>
        <Key id="reason_jobloss" value="Job loss without savings">Job loss or unstable employment without financial savings</Key>
        <Key id="homeless_reason_substance" value="Substance use challenges">Substance use challenges that affect employment and housing responsibilities</Key>
        <Key id="reason_wages" value="Low wages vs rising rents">Wages staying low while rents continue to rise</Key>
        <Key id="reason_discrimination" value="Racial discrimination in housing/lending">Racial discrimination in housing and lending markets</Key>
        <Key id="reason_assistance" value="Limited income support">Limited access to cash assistance or income-support programs</Key>
        <Key id="reason_weather" value="Unsheltered exposure to weather">Unsheltered people facing increased risks from extreme heat or severe weather</Key>
      </CheckboxInput>
    </Vertical>

